  "text": "In 18-month-old APOE4/4 mice, entorhinal cortex pyramidal neurons had more Rab5a-positive early endosomes and a higher endosome area fraction than APOE3/3 mice, with no difference in endosome size. This is class 5 because endosome morphology is not pH (reported: 11.7 vs 8.5 particles/cell).",
  "description": "APOE4/4 (85 neurons, 6 mice) vs APOE3/3 (118 neurons, 7 mice) targeted-replacement mice, 18 months, mixed sex; Rab5a immunofluorescence with Nissl co-stain, ImageJ particle analysis, Student's t-test. Caveat: aged mouse neurons, not human astrocytes; pH not measured.",
